ing blah  blah blah i i just think there's still a  lot of positives about this team i agree  with you completely this is a guy that  has played i think it was two full  seasons minimum of playoff games at  least 32 playoff games as of a couple of  years yeah right he's got a ton of  experience with the season riding on the  outcome of the game and there are other  guys in that locker room who have  playoff experience and there are veteran  players who may not have play of a  playoff experience per se but shaquille  barrett who was with the broncos when  they won super bowl 50 he said guys like  levante david even though they've never  played in the playoff game they get it  they understand that they know what it  takes to commence the process of  improving every week as you get closer  and closer to the postseason and they  recognize what is coming and i think  having a guy like brady around has a  tremendous  value  i just think at a certain point the  coaching staff just needs to get out of  the way and let it happen i just feel  like if anything they're getting in the  way of tom brady being tom brady  you know i i  it's definitely a little weird at times  there's no doubt i mean i i don't know  what to say either you're right i mean  it's just  i think they finally have figured it out  though i do  just the last few weeks i think they're  very close to really putting it together  the right way like even you know even  though the first half of the game this  past sunday wasn't good it wasn't like  some of the other first halves where  i've gone why are we in the shotgun and  throwing the ball every play like what  is going on it wasn't far off like i  said it was just like you know to bruce  erin's point they just didn't execute  quite as well as they would have liked  atlanta did some things to them i think  that caught them off guard and then once  they settled in okay they started  whooping butt and we're like an  unstoppable locomotive there but i i i i  do 